# Code search (ripgrep, which Claude Code's search uses) skips anything the root
# .gitignore lists, and the root .gitignore lists every codebase folder to keep
# the two git histories apart. Without the line below, a search started at the
# workspace root silently finds nothing inside the code. Git ignores this file's
# rules; search still honors the codebase's own .gitignore (node_modules stays
# out). One line per codebase, matching the root .gitignore.
!/{{APP_DIR}}/
